# The assets directory is the whole build output root (`./dist`), which also holds the
# Worker entry. An ignore list enumerating what to hide publishes every future root-level
# build artifact by default — a sourcemap or build-metadata file dropped there would ship
# with no review point. This inverts the default: ignore everything, then re-include only
# the files that are meant to be public. wrangler matches these with gitignore semantics
# (verified against wrangler 4.148.0: root-level strays are ignored, the three re-included
# paths are kept).
/*
!/logo.svg
!/favicon.ico
!/static
